From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:51:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: let a UI that changes the size keep the rest of the UI
 info

vnc, sdl2 and cocoa build the UI info they pass from nothing, so a
resize there also resets what another UI asked for: the refresh rate,
the physical size and the offsets. With a D-Bus client and a VNC client
on one console, a resize from the VNC client takes away the refresh rate
the D-Bus client gave, and the guest's EDID falls back to 75 Hz. gtk
and spice already start from the console's UI info.

Add qemu_console_set_ui_size() for a UI that knows only the size it
shows the console at, and use it in vnc, sdl2 and gtk. cocoa, which also
sets the physical size, the offsets and the refresh rate, starts from
the console's UI info instead; it started from an uninitialized one, and
passed whatever was on the stack as the refresh rate when it could not
read the screen's.

The test resizes the console from a VNC client, after a D-Bus client
gave a refresh rate.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
